{
  "id": "29268_hariageru",
  "headword": "{張|は}り{上|あ}げる",
  "reading": "はりあげる",
  "romaji": "hariageru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to raise (one's voice); to shout out",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to raise one's voice; to shout out; to belt out",
      "explanation": "To produce a loud, forceful voice, straining it so that it carries. Almost always used with {声|こえ} as the object, describing shouting, calling out, or singing loudly."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29268_hariageru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{大|おお}きな{声|こえ}を{張|は}り{上|あ}げた。",
      "english": "He raised his voice loudly.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29268_hariageru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{店員|てんいん}が{元気|げんき}よく{声|こえ}を{張|は}り{上|あ}げている。",
      "english": "The shop staff are calling out energetically.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29268_hariageru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{応援団|おうえんだん}は{試合|しあい}の{間|あいだ}ずっと{声|こえ}を{張|は}り{上|あ}げて{歌|うた}っていた。",
      "english": "The cheering squad sang at the top of their voices throughout the match.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Transitive verb, almost always taking {声|こえ} as its object: {声|こえ}を{張|は}り{上|あ}げる (to raise one's voice). Implies a deliberate, forceful effort to be loud, often to be heard over noise or distance.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {声|こえ}を{張|は}り{上|あ}げる: to raise one's voice; to shout\n- {大声|おおごえ}を{張|は}り{上|あ}げる: to yell loudly\n- {悲鳴|ひめい}を{張|は}り{上|あ}げる: to let out a scream\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {叫|さけ}ぶ: to shout — focuses on the cry itself; {張|は}り{上|あ}げる stresses the effort of forcing the voice out\n- {怒鳴|どな}る: to yell (angrily) — usually carries anger, which {張|は}り{上|あ}げる does not",
